WHY THIS BUILD EXISTS

The comment section on a post was redrawn to the structure in the owner's two
reference screenshots. It merged to staging (#236) and was then brought to main
as a NARROW CHERRY-PICK (#241, a168d886) rather than a promotion.

The cherry-pick is the whole point. main was 78 commits behind staging, last
promoted around 2026-09-04, and a full staging -> main merge would have carried
three weeks of unrelated work that nobody had reviewed — decided solo, at
night, to fire one build. So three commits were taken and nothing else:

  706f34b -> 900b55a   the sheet, search, flat rows, quick emoji
  51d2804 -> f4b069e   44px heart, the placeholder that fits 360px
  7e6d75b -> 8c6000d   row controls meet the tap floor, and the instrument

Each carries its `cherry picked from` line. The staging merge commit and #239's
baseline squash were deliberately excluded — main already had that correction
via #240. main is STILL 78 commits behind staging; this build does not change
that, and the promotion is still owed.

A cherry-pick across 78 commits can apply cleanly and still not work, so the
question actually checked was whether the redesign depended on anything that
exists only on staging. It does not: typecheck passed on main's codebase, and
so did the production lane build, which is the check that would catch something
surviving compile and failing at build.

WHAT THIS BUILD CARRIES

The app BUNDLES its web assets (capacitor.config.ts: webDir 'dist', no
server.url), so a web deploy alone reaches app members NEVER. That is why this
build exists rather than a deploy.

  - The comments surface is a bottom sheet at 78vh over the post, with the
    post still visible behind it. It was h-screen, which made it
    indistinguishable from a navigation: the photograph the comments are ABOUT
    disappeared on tap. The "Comments" title was sr-only and is now visible.
  - Search within the loaded thread. A matching parent keeps its replies; a
    non-matching parent is kept as context for the replies that did match.
  - Flat rows: name, badge and age on one line, text beneath, and the like
    moved out to a heart rail in the right margin with its count under it.
    That replaced a chat bubble whose corner badge overlapped the last line of
    text.
  - Replies stay indented under the comment they answer, with the reply box
    inline.
  - An eight-emoji quick row above the composer. A tap APPENDS to the draft and
    does not post: an instant post has no undo on a surface where the thumb is
    already moving, and appending keeps every comment on the one send path the
    keyword blocklist and the AI moderation call already guard.
  - The composer names the post's owner ("Add a comment for villagesqu…"),
    truncated to fit one line at 360px — measured in the harness after a
    capture showed it wrapping and being clipped.

