Build 1.2.10 - 2026-08-16 - THE CROP DIALOG WAS DEAF, AND EVERY MEASUREMENT I GAVE HIM WAS TRUE AND USELESS

  typecheck 0 · 1,865 tests pass · production build 0
  ZERO layout problems

VERSION IS 1.2.10. Build #99 carried 1.2.9 and this is different code.

THE ONE FAULT BEHIND ALL OF IT

Owner, on 1.2.9: "after uploadling any image clicked crop after that any of
option any fuction not wokring even not in web too, no cross, no mirror, no
moving the selection nothing - its like Screen is freezed - web and app."

The giveaway was "no cross". The close button is a plain <button onClick>. If
THAT is dead, nothing about cropping is wrong — the dialog is not receiving
input at all.

`WallPosts` renders `ImageCropModal` as a SIBLING of the composer's Radix
<Dialog>, and that dialog is open at the moment Crop is pressed. A Radix modal
makes the rest of the page inert while it is open by putting
`pointer-events: none` on <body>. This overlay lives outside the dialog's
content, so it inherited that — painted perfectly, laid out perfectly, and
completely deaf. Measured at 412px, hit-testing the centre of each control:

    crop dialog ALONE       body pointer-events auto   every control reachable
    behind the composer     body pointer-events NONE   Cancel, Close, 4:5,
                                                       Mirror — ALL DEAD
                            (the hit lands on Radix's own overlay)

One inherited CSS value. It explains every symptom he reported across three
rounds: no cross, no mirror, no rotate, no aspect chips, no drag, no pinch, no
zoom — on WEB and APP, because it was never a WebView difference at all.

WHY IT TOOK THREE BUILDS, stated plainly because it is the more important
lesson: all three crop scenes mount `ImageCropModal` ALONE. Alone it works, and
it has worked in every screenshot and every probe I ran. I reported those
numbers to him as evidence — "4:5 -> 190x238, never null", "pinch 100% -> 350%"
— and every one was true of a component nobody meets. THE BUG WAS IN THE
ARRANGEMENT, NOT THE COMPONENT. A harness that only ever renders things in
isolation certifies them in isolation.

`crop-modal-behind-dialog` reproduces the arrangement. With the fix, every
control is reachable and a real click moves the zoom 100% -> 125%. Without it,
all four tested controls are dead. That mutation is the proof.

WHAT ELSE CHANGED

 - `pointer-events-auto` on the crop dialog's root, pinned by a test.
 - Nothing else. The aspect-chip re-seed, the wheel zoom and the pinch
   pointercancel from 1.2.9 all stay — they were correct, they were simply
   unreachable behind a page that could not be touched.

WHAT ONLY THE PHONE CAN ANSWER

  1. Pick a photo, press Crop. Then press the X. It must close. That single tap
     is the whole test — if the X works, everything else in the dialog does.
  2. Then: drag the frame, tap 1:1 / 4:5 / Free / Reset, rotate, mirror, pinch,
     and on the website use the scroll wheel.
  3. Crop & Upload must send the part you framed, including after zooming.

STILL OPEN, AND NOT CLAIMED

 - Create Post from pages other than the Feed. My 1.2.9 "fix" for this was
   measured to change nothing and is recorded as such in the source. The
   owner's own instruction is the design answer — one uploader that opens where
   the member already is, with no navigation — and that is a change to make
   deliberately, not another guess.
 - The journal / featured-artist PDF cause. Instrumented, not fixed.
 - NO REELS. NO LIVE.

